# Label rows & collapsed sections

## Label + control on one row

When a **label** shares a row with controls (buttons, select, toggles, …) and width is tight:

1. Prefer **breaking the row** (`flex-wrap`) so the label and the control(s) land on **separate rows**.
2. Do **not** rely on label `word-break` / mid-word wrapping to keep them on one cramped line.

### Pattern

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — label wraps mid-word while controls stay beside it
<div className="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
  <label className="break-words">선택된 텍스트</label>
  <button>새로고침</button>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — wrap the row; keep label text intact
<div className="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-2 gap-y-1.5">
  <label className="shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap font-semibold …">선택된 텍스트</label>
  <div className="flex min-w-0 flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-1">
    <button>…</button>
  </div>
</div>
```

- Label: `shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap` (or truncate only when the label itself is a long path/title and truncation is intentional).
- Row: `flex flex-wrap` + `gap-x-* gap-y-*`.
- Controls group may use `flex-wrap` too for its own buttons.

## Collapsed disclosure sections

Collapsible blocks (system prompt, advanced settings, similar “접기” headers) must use a **distinct background when collapsed** so they are not mistaken for ordinary labels or static fields.

```tsx
// ✅ collapsed = tinted surface; expanded = neutral / open content
<button
  type="button"
  className={`flex w-full … rounded px-2 py-1.5 ${
    open
      ? 'bg-transparent'
      : 'bg-slate-300/90 dark:bg-slate-950/40'
  }`}
>
  …
</button>
```

- Apply the tint to the **collapsed header/chrome**, not only a text color change.
- Expanded state may drop the tint or keep a lighter border-only treatment; collapsed must stay visually distinct.

Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.
